  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.6,
      "end": 6.44,
      "text": "Five questions from the launch review your demo never shows."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.44,
      "end": 12.87,
      "text": "Each answer comes from a real test result in the repository."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.87,
      "end": 16.48,
      "text": "Question 1. Trust and access."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.48,
      "end": 23.69,
      "text": "Alice is signed in and asks for Bob's private project."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.69,
      "end": 30.18,
      "text": "In the flawed version, what does the server answer?"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.18,
      "end": 39.81,
      "text": "B: Bob's project, status 200."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.81,
      "end": 45.61,
      "text": "The server never checked who owns the project."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.61,
      "end": 48.21,
      "text": "Question 2. Duplicates."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.21,
      "end": 55.14,
      "text": "One click, a lost confirmation, an automatic retry."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.14,
      "end": 62.07,
      "text": "In the flawed version, how many orders exist?"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.07,
      "end": 69.91,
      "text": "B: two orders."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.91,
      "end": 76.65,
      "text": "With a unique key per purchase, the repair ends with one."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.65,
      "end": 82.12,
      "text": "Question 3. Data lifecycle."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.12,
      "end": 88.97,
      "text": "10,000 listings, 3,875 problems recorded."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.97,
      "end": 97.18,
      "text": "How many different listings were flagged?"
    },
    {
      "start": 103.18,
      "end": 105.88,
      "text": "B: 3,303 distinct listings."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.88,
      "end": 113.3,
      "text": "Some listings carry several flags. Ask which count a report shows."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.3,
      "end": 115.43,
      "text": "Question 4. Freshness."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.43,
      "end": 125.36,
      "text": "A green Live label, \"updated 0 s ago\". The sensor samples every 600 s."
    },
    {
      "start": 125.36,
      "end": 132.46,
      "text": "Just before the next sample, how old is the reading?"
    },
    {
      "start": 138.46,
      "end": 142.2,
      "text": "C: 570 seconds, nearly ten minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.2,
      "end": 147.82,
      "text": "The label described the page refresh, not the measurement."
    },
    {
      "start": 147.82,
      "end": 151.61,
      "text": "Question 5. Experience and speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 151.61,
      "end": 156.92,
      "text": "Flawed: 8 keystrokes, 17 requests, 12 rejected."
    },
    {
      "start": 156.92,
      "end": 164.5,
      "text": "After the repair, how many requests for the same typing?"
    },
    {
      "start": 170.5,
      "end": 172.07,
      "text": "C: one request."
    },
    {
      "start": 172.07,
      "end": 177.85,
      "text": "It waits for typing to pause and respects the retry delay."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.85,
      "end": 181.52,
      "text": "Ask for the test, not the demo."
    },
    {
      "start": 181.52,
      "end": 186.25,
      "text": "Ten questions and every fixture: the repository, linked below."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.25,
      "end": 189.92,
      "text": "Synthetic fixtures. Not an audit or certification."
    }
  ]
}